# M8/CTL-ASSET-01: an ALLOW-LIST, not a deny-list -- `*` refuses every
# path by default, and only the exact public surface below is handed
# back with `!`. A new root file or directory is therefore PRIVATE the
# moment it is added, with no further edit here, until someone
# deliberately negates it -- the opposite failure mode from a deny-list,
# where a new private file leaks until someone remembers to add it.
# Negation order matters (gitignore semantics): a directory must be
# negated before its children can be, and an un-negated path (e.g.
# portal/src, this repo's TypeScript-ish source for the portal's own
# build step) stays refused even though its parent is public.
# Proof: tests/foundation/assets-private.test.mjs (PIN-18).
*

!/index.html
!/404.html
!/gallery.html
!/register.html
!/glow.html
!/membership.html
!/membership-cancel.html
!/membership-success.html
!/robots.txt
!/sitemap.xml
!/llms.txt
!/_headers
!/_redirects

!/assets
!/assets/*
!/assets/events
!/assets/events/*
!/assets/features
!/assets/features/*
!/assets/gallery
!/assets/gallery/*
!/assets/hero
!/assets/hero/*
!/assets/services
!/assets/services/*

!/admin
!/admin/*

# Glow tournament signup (main 55c94ee..7b42600): glow.html and glow/list.html
# are static assets that main serves today. They must stay public, so the
# allow-list names them (tests/foundation/assets-private.test.mjs checks both).
!/glow
!/glow/*

# Portal additions (B1.13, A4/S-8, CTL-ASSET-01). The portal's own
# public UI lives under portal/ and IS served -- portal/src (the
# portal's Tailwind build input) is its one private sibling, and stays
# refused by simply never being negated below.
!/portal
!/portal/*

# FR3/SCV-05 (F-1): `!/portal/*` re-includes the directory entry
# `portal/src` itself even though nothing below ever negates its
# children -- a bare directory entry with no trailing slash still
# resolves as "served" for the one file directly inside it
# (`portal/src/input.css`, the Tailwind build input). Refusing the
# directory explicitly, after the negation above and before any of
# portal's other children are negated, closes that gap the same way
# the header comment already describes for an un-negated path.
# Proof: tests/foundation/assets-private.test.mjs (PIN-18).
/portal/src
/portal/src/*

!/portal/js
!/portal/js/*
!/portal/views
!/portal/views/*
!/portal/vendor
!/portal/vendor/*
